  "explains": "src/middleware.ts (the file beside the app and pages folders, the middleware of the project) now returns the session. Middleware runs before every request its matcher selects, and the matcher is not evaluated, so undecidable means affected: every screen of both routers and every route handler and API route is reached. That is fifteen screens (eleven App Router, four Pages Router) and eight routes (GET /api/health, GET and POST /api/orders, GET and DELETE /api/orders/{id}, GET /api/products, ANY /api/legacy/status, ANY /api/legacy/items/{id}), and past the http edges the three screens of the mobile client that call them: /orders, /orders/:orderId and /status. More than eight screens, so sample. The chain runs from the changed line to the declaration of the middleware function and on to the page's default export (or the method export of the route). All of them are listed here, 23 areas of the shop (a page with a slot page or an intercepting page, or with an optional catch-all, is one screen, with the other chains or paths shown) and the three client screens, and the test that recomputes the route table (test_nextjs_scenarios, nx_claims) says the list is the whole table.",
  "complete_for": [
    "changed_symbol",
    "caller",
    "screen",
    "route",
    "http_edge"
  ],
